    "result_text": "All 65 tests pass, including the new `Cp53Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the structured owner-created audit event as specified.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (new) \u2014 an immutable `record` with fields `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}`. It centralizes the \"current primary identifier\" in a single `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` method (returns `customerCode` today). This is the one place that changes when the customerCode is later unified into the `memberId` \u2014 the event will then carry the memberId with no other edits.\n\n2. **`EmitOwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (new) \u2014 an OfficeFloor step function that builds the event, stamping a **monotonically increasing** `seq` from a process-wide `AtomicLong`, serializes it to JSON (Jackson 3 `JsonMapper`), and logs it via the dedicated `AUDIT` logger \u2014 in addition to the existing human-readable audit line.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired a new `emitEvent` step between `audit` and `respond`, under the same `transaction` governance, so it runs after `save` (owner has its generated id) and after the audit line.\n\nThe emitted line looks like:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nI kept it as a separate step rather than folding it into `AuditOwnerCreated` to preserve the project's one-responsibility-per-function convention (the human-readable line and the machine-readable event are distinct concerns on the same `AUDIT` logger).",
